"""Results digest and reviewer-point map for the SAGMB R2 paper (Markdown).

Writes ``paper/r2/digest/results_digest.md`` (organised by the planned Results
subsections 5.1-5.10) and ``paper/r2/digest/reviewer_points.md`` (reviewer
points Q1-Q24 mapped to the evidence).

Rules implemented here
----------------------
* Every printed number is read from ``data/r2/tables/*.csv`` by a ``Fact``:
  CSV file + pandas row filter (``DataFrame.query``) + column (+ CI columns).
  The digest prints the provenance of every fact next to its value.
* Interpretive prose is a template that refers to facts by id (``{V[id]}`` =
  value, ``{C[id]}`` = value with interval); it contains no hand-typed numbers.
* A fact whose CSV, rows or column are missing is printed as ``MISSING`` and
  listed under "Problems"; the build never silently drops a fact.
* Analyses flagged ``post_hoc`` in the CSV (``analysis_status`` or
  ``post_hoc_columns``) are marked as such.
* Tables that other modules regenerate after 2026-10-14 11:30 (held-out,
  replication leave-k-out, tuning, posterior-mode tables) are checked for
  freshness; stale inputs are listed with the facts and assets that use them.

CLI: ``python -m r2.paper_assets.digest`` (with ``src`` on ``sys.path``) or
``python src/r2/make_paper_assets.py digest``.
"""
